{"kind": "finding", "id": "F-ghost-playback-013-01", "file": "Source/Parsek.Tests/PlaybackFidelityTests.cs", "line": 444, "method": "SteeringAngle_PointsIntoTheTurnAndClampsAtTheCaliperLimit", "category": "T3", "severity": "Medium", "confidence": "high", "falsifiability": "falsifiability: Source/Parsek/GhostPlaybackLogic.cs:5489; drop the leading minus in raw = -bodyRateDegPerSec * gain -> red", "what_it_asserts": "ComputeSynthDeflectionDegrees(-10, WheelSteeringGainDegPerDegPerSec, MaxWheelSteeringDegrees) is +15, and a -400 rate clamps to MaxWheelSteeringDegrees.", "why_weak": "The comment claims the cell pins the cancellation of the two inversions, but the caller-side negation lives at GhostPlaybackLogic.cs:5483 (-steeringHeadingRate) and is never called here; the test passes the post-negation value directly. Removing that minus would point ghost wheels the wrong way with the suite green.", "proposed_action": "Either reword the comment to claim only the helper's own sign and clamp, or add a cell that drives the steering path from a heading rate so the caller-side negate is covered.", "effort": "S", "july_ref": "none"}
{"kind": "coverage", "sut": "GhostPlaybackLogic", "sut_file": "Source/Parsek/GhostPlaybackLogic.cs", "sut_line": 5483, "case_kind": "mirror-direction", "proposed_name": "WheelSteering_PositiveHeadingRateProducesPositiveCaliperAngle", "sketch": "Drive the wheel-steering target through the production call shape (heading rate in, ComputeSynthDeflectionDegrees(-rate, WheelSteeringGainDegPerDegPerSec, MaxWheelSteeringDegrees)) for both signs of heading rate and assert the caliper angle points into the turn in each direction.", "guards": "Removal or duplication of the caller-side negation at GhostPlaybackLogic.cs:5483, which flips ghost wheel steering without reding any current cell.", "risk": "playback"}
